  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a Young&rsquo;s double slit experiment, two slits are illuminated with a light of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>. The line joining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>P</mi></math> is perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> as shown in the figure. If the first minimum is detected at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, the value of slits separation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;will be :</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1aa042d7-3e08-4c80-a366-e1c6d2bf4a87-9894890.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 197px;\" /></p><p>The distance of screen from slits <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
